{
  "slug": "chrome-extension-builder",
  "name": "Chrome Extension Builder",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Use when scaffolding, validating, testing, or publishing a Manifest V3 Chrome/Edge/Firefox extension. Builds end-to-end with WXT, Plasmo, or CRXJS — service-worker dispatcher, typed message passing, strict CSP, _locales/ i18n, Playwright smoke harness, Chrome Web Store submission prep.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **8 skills**, **3 agents**, **5 commands** and **3 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (8): `crxjs-vite` (Use when converting an existing Vite + React/Vue/Svelte project into a Chrome extension, or when the user explicitly…), `extension-architect` (Use when designing or auditing a Chrome/browser extension's architecture under Manifest V3), `extension-i18n` (Use when adding internationalization to a Chrome extension via `_locales/{locale}/messages.json` and `chrome.i18n.getMessage()`), `extension-publishing` (Use when preparing or executing a Chrome Web Store submission), `extension-security` (Use when implementing or auditing security-sensitive parts of a Chrome extension — content-script isolation, key/secret storage, CSP hardening,…), `extension-testing` (Use when setting up or running tests for a Chrome extension), `plasmo-framework` (Use when scaffolding or maintaining a Chrome extension with Plasmo (PlasmoHQ/plasmo)), `wxt-framework` (Use when scaffolding, configuring, building, or shipping a Chrome extension with WXT (wxt.dev))\n- **Agents** (3): `extension-architect` (Use when designing a new Chrome/browser extension architecture or evaluating an existing one), `extension-test-runner` (Use when running the build, lint, and Playwright smoke tests on a Chrome extension), `manifest-auditor` (Use when validating a Chrome extension manifest.json against Manifest V3 schema, Chrome Web Store policy, and security best…)\n- **Commands** (5): `add-feature` (Add a surface (popup, options, side panel, content script, devtools panel, background handler) to an existing Chrome extension), `migrate-mv2` (Audit a Manifest V2 extension and produce an MV3 migration plan with concrete patches), `new` (Scaffold a new production-ready Chrome (MV3) extension), `publish` (Prepare Chrome Web Store submission — generate listing assets, run final checks, build the zip, optionally upload via…), `validate` (Run all validators on the current Chrome extension directory — manifest schema, permissions, CSP, web-ext lint)\n- **Hooks** (3): `PostToolUse`, `PreToolUse`, `UserPromptSubmit`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install chrome-extension-builder@claude-community` from `harry-harish/chrome-extension-builder`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
